; ============================================================
; Conway's Game of Life  —  STELLAR  (VM1 @ $4000)
; ============================================================
; ASCII cellular automaton.  40x20 live grid, double-buffered, bordered
; (stride 42 = W+2 so the 8 neighbour offsets are constant and the dead
; 1-cell border absorbs the edges -- no per-cell bounds checks).
;
; Seed: 2 gliders (travel down-right) + 2 blinkers + a toad (both period-2
; oscillators) + a block (still life).  Runs 24 generations then HALTs,
; redrawing in place via ANSI clear+home (ESC[2J ESC[H).  Best on an ANSI/VT
; terminal; on a non-ANSI terminal the frames just scroll.  Fits an 80x24 screen.
;
; Multitasking off (C7 00) so VM1 owns the grids in its RAM:
;   GRID_A rel $1000 (real $5000)   GRID_B rel $1400 (real $5400)   924 B each.
;
; Base V0061.22 firmware only (SEROUTI $CA, shift/math ops, FILLMEMXY $FB,
; DLYI $C0).  Ends with the F0 00 00 pre-pass marker.
;
; SPEED: inter-frame pause is DLYI (`C0 40`).  Raise/lower the $40 operand to taste
;   (sites: $4133, $4287, $43D9).
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/gol.py, real V0061.22 sim): gen 1 matches
;   hand-computed Life (blinker H->V, block still-life stable, glider->phase 2)
;   at stride 42; 40x20 grid renders all seeds correctly.
;
; Code $4000..$43EB (1004 B).
; ============================================================

